-- =============================================================
-- Costmatic — Urdu names for the seeded catalog (1150 products)
--
-- The catalog seeds insert with an empty name_ur. This fills it in, matching
-- on the English name, so a freshly seeded database ends up the same as the
-- shop's. Run AFTER catalog_beverages_pakistan.sql and catalog_kirana_pakistan.sql.
--
--   psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f supabase/seeds/urdu_names_backfill.sql
--
-- Only fills blanks — a name the shopkeeper has already written by hand is
-- never overwritten, so this is safe to re-run.
--
-- On the naming: Western digits are kept ("100 گرام", not "۱۰۰ گرام") because
-- the shopkeeper types 100 to search, and the size is what they search by.
-- Brand names that have no settled Urdu spelling stay in Latin — that is how
-- they appear on the pack and on the shelf label.
-- =============================================================

do $ur$
declare
